; =============================================================================
; R9 review fixes — authorization bypass + stranding/fork paths from the
; round-9 adversarial review of feat/auto-reconnect (PROTO-001 Principle 12).
; =============================================================================
;
; Findings under repair (reviewer IDs → tasks):
;
;   P1 group.rs:783    sender-controlled :for roster can filter the true owner
;                      out of the REQ-012b pre-add election      → task-f1
;   P1 session.rs:1307 carve-out commit discards the Welcome for pending Adds,
;                      stranding the added leaf                  → task-f23
;   P1 session.rs:1314 carve-out frame carries one evidence object while the
;                      commit covers every pending Remove → fork → task-f23
;   P1 session.rs:712  FanPending drains only on Handled events; Dropped-only
;                      traffic wedges sends at NotReady forever  → task-f4
;   P2 session.rs:813  transient (Storage) welcome failures are receipt-acked;
;                      hub deletes its only RAM copy → stranded  → task-f5
;   P2 chat.rs:1051    socket close leaves queued send_rx frames unresolved
;                      through the whole outage                  → task-f6
;
; Fix designs (agreed against SPEC-013 v0.10.0 + SPEC-024):
;
;   f1  The joiner can never verify which leaves a commit added (the :for list
;       is sender-supplied metadata; SPEC-024 REQ-010 gives the cross-check to
;       MEMBERS, who see the commit — never to the joiner). So authority must
;       not derive from it: (i) when the genesis creator is a live leaf of the
;       delivered tree (minus the joiner's own leaf), the Welcome sender MUST
;       be the creator (handle AND key) — co-added claims are irrelevant to
;       the election, since Adds only grow the tree and creator-preferred
;       election ignores extra leaves; (ii) when the creator is NOT a live
;       pre-add leaf (owner-departure world), a multi-add Welcome (:for
;       naming anyone besides the joiner) is REJECTED fail-closed — the
;       co-added roster is unverifiable exactly where it would decide the
;       election — and a single add elects lex-smallest over tree-minus-joiner,
;       which IS the pre-add roster. Closes the bypass with zero trust in :for.
;
;   f23 Scope the owner-departure carve-out commit to the owner's OWN
;       self-Remove proposal(s): remove every other pending proposal from the
;       local store (openmls remove_pending_proposal) before
;       commit_to_pending_proposals. Uncovered proposals are epoch-scoped and
;       die at the merge on every peer anyway; their proposers re-drive at the
;       new epoch (REQ-014 retry semantics, presence/keyready re-drives). The
;       scoped commit produces no Welcome (nothing is added — no stranded
;       leaf) and covers exactly the Remove its single :evidence validates
;       (no fork). Defensively refuse to fan if a Welcome is still produced.
;
;   f4  Hand the recovered FanPending batch to the caller on EVERY event, not
;       only Handled: new public MlsSession::take_recovered_fanout() drained
;       by chat.rs after every handle_frame outcome and after a NotReady
;       encrypt_outbound refusal; the existing Handled prepend keeps batch-
;       before-own-frames ordering (drain is idempotent — second take empty).
;
;   f5  Ack a failed first-contact welcome ONLY on MlsError::Rejected (a
;       deterministic validation refusal — redelivery can never succeed).
;       Storage/Stack/NotReady failures return Dropped un-acked so the hub
;       queue redelivers once the transient clears (REQ-013 leaves the init
;       key intact on failed joins, so the retry can still consume it).
;
;   f6  On entering reconnect (and on every backoff iteration), drain send_rx
;       with try_recv and resolve each queued OutboundFrame with
;       OutboundReject::reconnecting — the same verdict new sends already get
;       from the store's Reconnecting state; closes the enqueue race.

(meta plan
  (title "R9 review fixes — welcome election authority, carve-out scoping, drain paths")
  (status "active")
  (description
    "Repair the six round-9 review findings: REQ-012b election over a "
    "sender-controlled roster, carve-out commits that strand added leaves or "
    "fork on multi-Remove evidence, FanPending wedging on Dropped-only "
    "traffic, transient welcome failures being receipt-acked, and queued "
    "sends left unresolved across a socket close.")
  (created "2026-07-22")
  (branch "feat/auto-reconnect"))

(given agent-hugo-available)

(given task-f1)     ; group.rs — REQ-012b election without sender-controlled roster
(given task-f23)    ; session.rs — scope the carve-out commit to the owner self-Remove
(given task-f4)     ; session.rs + chat.rs — drain FanPending on every event
(given task-f5)     ; session.rs — ack only deterministic welcome rejections
(given task-f6)     ; chat.rs — resolve queued sends on socket close
(given task-verify) ; regression tests + build + clippy + full suite + commit

(meta task-f1
  (description
    "Rewrite validate_staged_welcome (src/mls/group.rs): never filter the "
    "pre-add roster by the sender-supplied co_added list. Creator-live → "
    "sender must be the creator by handle+key; creator not a live pre-add "
    "leaf → reject multi-add welcomes fail-closed, elect lex-smallest over "
    "tree-minus-joiner for a single add. Drop the co_added parameter from "
    "validate_staged_welcome/join_from_welcome if it becomes authority-unused "
    "(the :for list stays load-bearing for addressing/acks in session.rs). "
    "Update the round-8 multi-add test to the new rule and add the attack "
    "regression: a non-owner member authors a valid Add and lists the true "
    "owner in :for — the join MUST be rejected.")
  (acceptance
    "1. cargo test -p hark mls::group passes. 2. New regression test: "
    "attacker-authored welcome naming the owner as co-added is rejected with "
    "the REQ-012b reason. 3. Bootstrap add, steady-state creator add, and "
    "creator-live multi-add still join. 4. Post-departure single add by the "
    "interim owner still joins; post-departure multi-add is rejected."))

(meta task-f23
  (description
    "In MlsSession::maybe_commit_owner_departure (src/mls/session.rs): before "
    "commit_to_pending_proposals, remove every pending proposal that is NOT a "
    "Remove of the owner's leaf proposed by the owner (reuse the "
    "covers_owner_self_remove predicate shape); refuse to proceed (warn + "
    "empty) if the scoped commit still returns Some(welcome). The single "
    ":evidence then validates every Remove the commit covers.")
  (acceptance
    "1. Regression test: with a pending foreign Add + the owner self-Remove "
    "stored, the carve-out commit removes ONLY the owner; peers accept the "
    "frame and the added-leaf welcome is never fanned half-baked (the Add "
    "dies with the epoch). 2. Test: with a second evidenced Remove pending, "
    "the carve-out commit covers only the owner self-Remove and every peer "
    "accepts it against the bye evidence."))

(meta task-f4
  (description
    "session.rs: make take_rebroadcast reachable from the caller on every "
    "event — pub(crate) take_recovered_fanout(). chat.rs run_connection: "
    "after handle_frame outcomes other than Handled, and after a NotReady "
    "encrypt refusal on the send arm, drain and transmit the recovered batch "
    "(shared send-batch helper; write failure exits HubClosed as everywhere).")
  (acceptance
    "1. Regression test at the session level: a FanPending session receiving "
    "only a Dropped-producing frame hands the batch out and unlocks mutation "
    "(encrypt_outbound succeeds afterwards). 2. Existing round-8 FanPending "
    "tests still pass (Handled ordering preserved)."))

(meta task-f5
  (description
    "session.rs on_welcome: split the error arm — ack + Handled only for "
    "MlsError::Rejected; Storage/Stack/NotReady return Dropped with no ack "
    "so the hub redelivers after the transient clears. The group-established "
    "redelivery/rival arm keeps acking as today.")
  (acceptance
    "1. Test: a first-contact welcome failing with Rejected (garbage ct) "
    "still acks (round-8 behaviour). 2. Test: a Storage-class failure does "
    "NOT ack and returns Dropped."))

(meta task-f6
  (description
    "chat.rs reconnect(): after mark_reconnecting and again inside each "
    "backoff iteration, drain self.send_rx via try_recv, resolving every "
    "queued OutboundFrame's result_tx with OutboundReject::reconnecting and "
    "the outage detail.")
  (acceptance
    "1. Test: a frame queued into send_rx before/while the socket closes is "
    "resolved with the Reconnecting reject once reconnect() runs, not left "
    "pending. 2. Existing reconnect tests unaffected."))

(meta task-verify
  (description
    "Red-gate check per fix (each new regression test observed failing "
    "against the pre-fix code where practical), then cargo build, cargo "
    "clippy --all-targets, cargo test. Commit as round-9 hardening with the "
    "finding-by-finding summary.")
  (acceptance
    "Clean build, clean clippy, full suite green, one commit on "
    "feat/auto-reconnect describing all six repairs."))

; Dependencies: the five fixes are independent; verification needs them all.
(given verify-needs-fixes)

(normally r-ready-f1 task-f1 ready-f1)
(normally r-ready-f23 task-f23 ready-f23)
(normally r-ready-f4 task-f4 ready-f4)
(normally r-ready-f5 task-f5 ready-f5)
(normally r-ready-f6 task-f6 ready-f6)

(normally r-ready-verify
  (and task-verify verify-needs-fixes
       completed-f1 completed-f23 completed-f4 completed-f5 completed-f6)
  ready-verify)

(normally r-assign-f1 (and ready-f1 agent-hugo-available) assign-to-f1-hugo)
(normally r-assign-f23 (and ready-f23 agent-hugo-available) assign-to-f23-hugo)
(normally r-assign-f4 (and ready-f4 agent-hugo-available) assign-to-f4-hugo)
(normally r-assign-f5 (and ready-f5 agent-hugo-available) assign-to-f5-hugo)
(normally r-assign-f6 (and ready-f6 agent-hugo-available) assign-to-f6-hugo)
(normally r-assign-verify (and ready-verify agent-hugo-available) assign-to-verify-hugo)

